<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Without this the CarPlay scene declared in Info.plist never activates,
       however correct the delegate is.

       It stayed out of this file until Apple's grant landed, because an
       entitlement the App ID does not carry does not warn — it fails the
       archive outright: "Entitlement com.apple.developer.carplay-audio not
       found and could not be included in profile."

       The grant is only half of it. The App ID has to be given the capability
       by hand, and no API can do it: App Store Connect's writable
       `capabilityType` enumeration has 28 values and none of them is CarPlay
       (the server itself will list them if you send an invalid one). It is a
       checkbox, under Identifiers -> the App ID -> Capabilities -> "CarPlay
       Audio App (CarPlay framework)". Ticked 2026-08-31; the API now reports
       CARPLAY_PLAYABLE_CONTENT on the App ID. -->
  <key>com.apple.developer.carplay-audio</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>group.com.benjaminissa.issareader</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
